    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.base16\n\n### Description\n\nHi 👋 ,\r\n\r\nThank you for these great plugins!\r\n\r\nOnce thing I miss in [mini.base16]([mini.base16](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.base16)) is **syntax highlighting** in diffs.\r\n\r\nConsider this example in [tokyonight](https://github.com/folke/tokyonight.nvim):\r\n![Screenshot 2023-02-26 at 11 54 02](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1009936/221406124-81674716-8255-4507-9a86-a8a91b3c45a7.png)\r\n\r\nNow the same in [mini.base16](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.base16):\r\n![Screenshot 2023-02-26 at 11 54 53](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1009936/221406181-f5bda154-968c-4fe4-9146-4e5f80171673.png)\r\n\r\nIn [tokyonight](https://github.com/folke/tokyonight.nvim), syntax highlighting is still active, e.g. for additions. In [mini.base16](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.base16), it's just green text.\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to keep syntax highlighting in diffs and only change the background of additions/substractions/changes?\r\n\r\nThanks again and best regards,\r\nDavid\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
