        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yeah, this is indeed a severe limitation of 'base16'. All \"colorful colors\" are intended to be used as foreground. For background there are simply 4 shades available. There is simply not enough colors to both preserve original syntax highlighting and and make background green/red/purple, as this might lead to same colors for text and background.\r\n\r\nLack of shades in colors (both accent ones and darker shades of background) is the main reason why I plan to make 'mini.base3' (name can vary) - my own color scheme generator where I can make any shades I want.\r\n\r\nThe only solution to this is to switch background to be colorful instead. This will not preserve highlighting, unfortunately. Here is how it will look:\r\n\r\n![screenshot_2023-02-26_13:48:55](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/24854248/221409019-6fdbfef6-fa17-42a5-92ce-1e1a5879efa2.png)\r\n\r\nWhat do you think about this?",
