            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I think depending on the color scheme, it might be too bright/intrusive.\r\n\r\nAgree.\r\n\r\n> My initial thought was to take the given background color of mini.base16 (`base00`) and slightly modify it to make it more red/green/yellow. But I'm not sure if that would work.\r\n\r\nYes, it would be great and this is what I plan to do in my own color scheme generator. But this can't be part of 'mini.base16', unfortunately, because it would mean creation of a color outside of supplied palette.\r\n\r\nSo I think I'll close it with a promise to use your suggestion in an upcoming original color scheme generator in some near-ish future.\r\n\r\nThanks for your interest and promotion of 'mini.nvim'.",
