        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "By the way, @David-Kunz, I forgot to write here after I released new color scheme: [mini.hues](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-hues.md). Making sure that diffs highlight only background was one of the first things I did when started tweaking highlight groups :)\r\n\r\nHere are some examples of diffs using 'randomhue' color scheme:\r\n\r\n![demo_mini-hues_diff_1](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/24854248/532779cc-18cc-4fbb-84fe-14e6886d5e27)\r\n![demo_mini-hues_diff_2](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/24854248/7966e346-68f4-4105-b75f-be77858b09b3)\r\n![demo_mini-hues_diff_3](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/24854248/5e9dbd69-ff26-4ded-b8c1-295436e2fdb5)\r\n\r\nGranted, background is not always clearly differentiable, but it is not always easy to procedurally generate very different background color. Like `DiffAdd` will have green background which can't be *very* different from already green `Normal` background (but it is as different as it reasonably can be).",
